@event enrolment
# en: Enrolment
title [cbadef] = 选课
# en: {term_index == 1: Your first term. The registrar slides a list across the desk: four courses open to first-years.|A new term, and a new list. Courses you've passed are gone from it; new levels have appeared.} {member(thesis): Choose one; the thesis takes your other slot.|Choose two.} Course fees are eight crowns.
text [3119c3] = {term_index == 1: 你的第一个学期。教务员把一张清单推过桌面：四门对一年级开放的课。|新学期，新清单。你已通过的课不见了，新的级别冒了出来。}{member(thesis): 选一门；毕业论文占了你另一个名额。|选两门。}课程费八克朗。
# en: The registrar's hall at the start of term, students queueing at long tables with course lists that rewrite themselves.
scene [6d30e9] = 开学时的教务大厅，学生们在长桌前排队，手里的课程表会自己改写。
# en: There is nothing left for you to take
opt.none.label [b606eb] = 没有你能选的课了
# en: The registrar checks the list twice. Nothing on it is open to you this term. "Enjoy the quiet," she says, without much conviction.
opt.none.say.1 [3ba6f1] = 教务员把名单核对了两遍。这学期上面没有一门课对你开放。“享受清静吧。”她说，语气不太确定。

@event club_fair_v3
# en: The Club Fair
title [ce4fee] = 社团招新会
# en: The Club Fair fills the courtyard. Every table wants you; every captain swears theirs is the one that matters. {rel(lyra) >= 6: Lyra is at the Duelling Circle's table, pretending not to watch which way you walk.|}
text [fa6309] = 社团招新会挤满了庭院。每张桌子都想要你，每位社长都发誓自家才是最要紧的。{rel(lyra) >= 6: 莱拉站在决斗社的桌边，假装没在看你往哪儿走。|}
# en: The courtyard full of recruiting tables, banners snapping, a duelling demonstration drawing a crowd.
scene [72616b] = 庭院里摆满招新桌，旗帜猎猎作响，一场决斗示范引来一圈围观者。
# en: {member(club): Stay with your club|Not this year}
opt.none.label [9e77c4] = {member(club): 留在你的社团|今年算了}
# en: {member(club): Another year with the same table.|You can join at next year's fair.}
opt.none.hint [5c873f] = {member(club): 和同一张桌子再过一年。|明年的招新会还能加入。}
# en: {member(club): {~You stop by your own club's table to help hand out leaflets. Someone asks you if it's worth joining. You say yes and mean it.|You walk past every other table with the ease of someone already spoken for.}|You collect three leaflets and a free biscuit, and sign nothing.}
opt.none.say.1 [b61f4a] = {member(club): {~你在自己社团的桌边帮忙发传单。有人问你值不值得加入。你说值得，而且是真心的。|你从别的桌子前走过，带着一种名花有主的从容。}|你领了三张传单和一块免费饼干，什么也没签。}
# en: Resign from your club
opt.quit.label [990542] = 退出你的社团
# en: You can join again at next year's fair, as a new member.
opt.quit.hint [5bb00e] = 明年的招新会还能以新成员身份重新加入。
# en: {~You hand back your club pin at the table where you got it. It feels smaller than it did.|You resign. Your evenings are yours again, and nobody will expect you anywhere.}
opt.quit.say.1 [0a0a06] = {~你在当初领徽章的那张桌子前把社团徽章交了回去。它看起来比当时小了。|你退出了。晚上又归你自己了，也没人会在哪儿等你。}

@event job_board_visit
# en: The Job Board
title [377c1b] = 招工告示板
# en: Notices for work, three layers deep: the library, the Gilded Newt, Pell & Daughters, the courier loft. Each wants someone reliable. Each says so twice.
text [358cb2] = 招工启事叠了三层：图书馆、镀金蝾螈酒馆、佩尔父女药铺、信使阁楼。每家都要个靠得住的人，每家都说了两遍。
# en: A cork board crowded with notices, a student running a finger down a column of shift times.
scene [62cc7b] = 一块挤满告示的软木板，一名学生用手指顺着一列排班时间往下划。
# en: Just looking
opt.look.label [4af612] = 只是看看
# en: You read every notice twice and take none of them down.
opt.look.say.1 [5234e4] = 你把每张告示都读了两遍，一张也没揭下来。
# en: Hand in your notice
opt.quit.label [e9edc6] = 递交辞呈
# en: You can find work again later.
opt.quit.hint [974ede] = 以后还能再找工作。
# en: You hand in your notice. Your evenings are yours again; so is your empty purse.
opt.quit.say.1 [3dd0ab] = 你递交了辞呈。晚上又归你自己了，空荡荡的钱袋也是。

@event break_plan
# en: The Break
title [e3e693] = 假期
# en: {month == 5: The winter break.|The summer break.} Two months without lectures. The castle empties, mostly.
text [78e780] = {month == 5: 冬假。|暑假。}两个月没有课。城堡几乎空了。
# en: The academy gates thrown open, barges loading trunks, a few students lingering on the steps with nowhere they'd rather be.
scene [003006] = 学院大门敞开，驳船装着行李箱，几个学生在台阶上逗留，哪儿也不想去。
# en: Stay at the castle
opt.castle.label [04365a] = 留在城堡
# en: Quiet corridors and secrets. Board 8 crowns a month.
opt.castle.hint [6c24c3] = 安静的走廊和秘密。每月食宿 8 克朗。
# en: The castle in the holidays is a different building: louder echoes, kinder staff, doors you've never seen open.
opt.castle.say.1 [f9e1bd] = 假期里的城堡是另一座建筑：回声更响，职员更和气，还有你从没见开过的门。
# en: Go home
opt.home.label [c93952] = 回家
# en: Family, old friends, free board.
opt.home.hint [1bbb35] = 家人、老朋友、免费食宿。
# en: The barge, the coach, the last mile on foot. Home is smaller than you remember, and warmer.
opt.home.say.1 [0b9342] = 驳船、马车，最后一里路靠双脚。家比记忆中小，也比记忆中暖。
# en: Work on campus
opt.work.label [2ebfbe] = 留校打工
# en: A holiday gig that pays well. Board 8 crowns a month.
opt.work.hint [6b010a] = 一份工钱不错的假期零工。食宿每月 8 克朗。
# en: You trade the holidays for wages. Your feet will remember it.
opt.work.say.1 [e054a1] = 你用假期换了工钱。你的脚会记住这一切。
# en: Start your internship
opt.intern.label [744abc] = 开始实习
# en: A stipend, a supervisor and a project.
opt.intern.hint [abd74b] = 一份津贴、一位导师和一个课题。
# en: You pack a trunk of notebooks and set off {member(intern_expedition): up the long road to the high plateau|{member(intern_field_station): across the moors to the field station|{member(intern_thornwick): on the coach to Thornwick, of all places|on the long coach to the capital}}}.
opt.intern.say.1 [db63d2] = 你装了一箱笔记本，{member(intern_expedition): 踏上去高原的漫长山路|{member(intern_field_station): 穿过荒原前往野外站|{member(intern_thornwick): 坐上去荆木学院的马车，偏偏是那儿|坐上去王都的长途马车}}}。

@event course_exam
# en: Exam Day
title [482384] = 考试日
# en: Exam day for {track}. The hall is silent except for quills and somebody's knee bouncing under a desk. {~The paper is long.|The first question is one you revised.|The first question is one you didn't.|The invigilator turns the hourglass with a click you feel in your teeth.}
text [6e3a75] = {track}考试日。考场里鸦雀无声，只有羽毛笔的沙沙声，还有谁的膝盖在桌下抖个不停。{~试卷很长。|第一道题正好是你复习过的。|第一道题恰好是你没复习的。|监考老师把沙漏一翻，那一声咔哒你连牙齿都感觉得到。}
# en: A silent exam hall in late light, rows of bent heads, an hourglass on the invigilator's desk.
scene [43a564] = 傍晚光线里寂静的考场，一排排低着的头，监考桌上放着一只沙漏。
# en: Answer what you know, carefully
opt.left.label [7dfdbe] = 稳扎稳打，写你会的
# en: {~You write slowly: everything you're sure of, and nothing you aren't.|You check every answer twice and hand in at the bell.}
opt.left.say.1 [a7c6e9] = {~你写得很慢：有把握的都写上，没把握的一个字也不写。|你每道题都检查两遍，铃响才交卷。}
# en: Go for top marks
opt.right.label [4d6661] = 冲击高分
# en: {~You take the hardest question first and gamble the essay on an idea you had at breakfast.|You write the answer you'd want to read, not the safe one.}
opt.right.say.1 [b27304] = {~你先做最难的题，把整篇论述押在早饭时冒出的一个想法上。|你写下自己想读的答案，而不是稳妥的那个。}

@event track_warning
# en: A Word About Your Attendance
title [6bd5a3] = 关于你的出勤
# en: A note about {track}: your attendance and your efforts have slipped, and it has been noticed. One more term like this and there will be consequences.
text [2da6ae] = 一张关于{track}的便条：你的出勤和努力都在下滑，有人注意到了。再这样一个学期，就要有后果了。
# en: A folded note on official paper, the words "performance" and "concern" underlined twice.
scene [7cac89] = 一张折起来的公文纸，“表现”和“关切”两个词下面各划了两道线。
# en: Promise to do better
opt.left.label [cba502] = 保证会改进
# en: You write back a promise in your neatest hand. Now you'll have to keep it.
opt.left.say.1 [5983e6] = 你用最工整的字回了一份保证。现在你得兑现它了。
# en: Let it slide
opt.right.label [344baa] = 随它去
# en: You put the note in a drawer and skip the next session to prove a point. The note doesn't stop existing in the drawer.
opt.right.say.1 [4ea3c0] = 你把便条塞进抽屉，还故意翘掉了下一次，以示态度。便条在抽屉里也照样存在。

@event job_term_review
# en: Another Term?
title [9e843b] = 再干一学期？
# en: The term is over, and so is the rota for {track}. A fresh one goes up for next term, and there's a gap where your name usually goes. {~Nobody would blame you either way.|Your feet have an opinion. So does your purse.|Someone has already pencilled a question mark next to it.}
text [7bad94] = 学期结束了，{track}的排班表也到头了。下学期的新表会贴出来，你平常写名字的地方空着一格。{~怎么选都没人会怪你。|你的脚有意见。你的钱袋也有。|已经有人在旁边用铅笔画了个问号。}
# en: A staff rota pinned to a door, last term's names crossed off, a blank column waiting for next term's.
scene [2d74da] = 门上钉着一张员工排班表，上学期的名字都划掉了，空出一栏等着下学期。
# en: Stay on next term
opt.left.label [7e4424] = 下学期继续干
# en: {~You write your name in the gap. Another term of shifts, another term of wages.|Your name goes back on the rota, in ink this time.}
opt.left.say.1 [46037e] = {~你在空格里写上名字。又一学期的班，又一学期的工钱。|你的名字回到了排班表上，这次用的是墨水。}
# en: Resign
opt.right.label [b07941] = 辞职
# en: {~You hand in your notice, politely. The evenings are yours again; the purse is lighter for it.|You leave the gap empty. You can always find work again, if you need to.}
opt.right.say.1 [599e30] = {~你客客气气地递了辞呈。晚上又归你了；钱袋也因此轻了。|你让那一格空着。真需要的话，总还能再找活干。}

@event track_promotion
# en: A Step Up
title [39f03f] = 更上一层
# en: {track} wants to promote you. More responsibility, more respect, and in the right places, more pay.
text [a932cb] = {track}想提拔你。更多责任，更多尊重，在某些地方，还有更多薪水。
# en: A small ceremony in a cramped room, someone pinning a badge to a student's collar while the others applaud.
scene [c03b55] = 狭小房间里的一场小仪式，有人把徽章别在一名学生的领口上，其他人鼓掌。
# en: Accept
opt.left.label [b26149] = 接受
# en: The badge is a little crooked. You don't straighten it.
opt.left.say.1 [7c4086] = 徽章有点歪。你没去扶正它。
# en: Not yet
opt.right.label [8dd27c] = 还不是时候
# en: "When you're ready, then." They mean it. The offer will come again.
opt.right.say.1 [ffa0ad] = “那就等你准备好。”他们是认真的。这个机会还会再来。

@event intern_application
# en: Applications Open
title [e7df06] = 开始申请
# en: Summer research posts are open. Six notices, six seals, six lists of requirements. Apply to as many as you like: the first letter is an evening's work, and every one after it costs another evening and the postage.
text [c4837d] = 夏季研究岗位开放申请了。六张告示，六枚火漆，六份要求清单。想申请几个都行：第一封信花你一个晚上，之后每多一封，就再搭上一个晚上和邮费。
# en: A cluster of notices with wax seals pinned above all the others: summer research posts, each with its own demands.
scene [a45b3c] = 一簇盖着火漆的告示钉在所有告示上方：夏季研究岗位，各有各的要求。
# en: The Royal Library
opt.royal.label [64f580] = 皇家图书馆
# en: GPA 2.5, an interview on lore, a love of indexes.
opt.royal.hint [fbd651] = GPA 2.5，学识面试，以及对索引的热爱。
# en: {member(intern_royal_library): They've already asked you back.|Needs Astromancy II.}
opt.royal.locked [c8e0b8] = {member(intern_royal_library): 他们已经请你回去了。|需要星象与占卜 II。}
# en: {~Another letter, another evening, another stamp. Your hand aches in a very particular place.|You write it once, cross out half, write it again. The postage comes out of your own purse.}
opt.royal.say.1 [69905a] = {~又一封信，又一个晚上，又一张邮票。你的手在一个非常特定的地方发酸。|你写了一遍，划掉一半，又写一遍。邮费从你自己的钱袋里出。}
# en: You write the letter three times and send the best one. Probably the best one.
opt.royal.say.2 [b67a70] = 信你写了三遍，寄出了最好的一封。大概是最好的一封。
# en: You write the letter, and then find you can't pay the postage. It stays on your desk.
opt.royal.say.3 [ccb58d] = 你写好了信，却发现付不起邮费。它只能留在你桌上。
