# en: Not this year
opt.none.label [594ecf] = 今年算了
# en: You let the notices flap. There's always next year, until there isn't.
opt.none.say.1 [cd2444] = 你任由告示在风里拍打。总还有明年——直到没有为止。

@event intern_offer
# en: Letters With Seals
title [51ad68] = 盖着火漆的信
# en: The spring post brings answers. {applied(internship): There are sealed letters on your desk. Which do you open first?|There are no more sealed letters.} {guile >= 35 and rel(isolde) >= 6 and not member(intern_unseen_office): There is also a plain grey envelope you never asked for.|}
text [7b4927] = 春天的邮件带来了回音。{applied(internship): 你的书桌上放着几封封了火漆的信。先拆哪一封？|再没有封着火漆的信了。}{guile >= 35 and rel(isolde) >= 6 and not member(intern_unseen_office): 还有一只你从没申请过的素灰色信封。|}
# en: Heavy envelopes with wax seals on a dormitory desk, one of them plain grey with no seal at all.
scene [28d6f5] = 宿舍书桌上放着几只封着火漆的厚信封，其中一只是素灰色的，根本没有封漆。
# en: Letter from the Royal Library
opt.royal.label [04415c] = 皇家图书馆的来信
# en: They asked for a GPA of 2.5. The interview tests lore.
opt.royal.hint [693412] = 他们要求 GPA 2.5。面试考学识。
# en: "We are pleased." You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer in the oldest archives in the realm.
opt.royal.say.1 [d43827] = “我们很高兴。”你把信读了一遍又一遍，直到火漆裂开。一整个夏天，待在王国最古老的档案馆里。
# en: "We regret." The interview went well, they write, and not quite well enough.
opt.royal.say.2 [4db135] = “我们很遗憾。”信上说，你的面试表现不错，只是还差一点。
# en: "We regret." They wanted a GPA of 2.5, and they say so twice.
opt.royal.say.3 [ee2e12] = “我们很遗憾。”他们要的是 GPA 2.5，而且说了两遍。
# en: Letter from the Conclave
opt.conclave.label [187867] = 七塔议会的来信
# en: They asked for a GPA of 3.0. The interview tests arcana. A word from Thorne would help.
opt.conclave.hint [e87947] = 他们要求 GPA 3.0。面试考奥术。有索恩的一句推荐会更好。
# en: "We are pleased." You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer in spell research under the Seven Towers.
opt.conclave.say.1 [b0dd08] = “我们很高兴。”你把信读了一遍又一遍，直到火漆裂开。一整个夏天，在七塔之下研究法术。
# en: "We regret." The interview went well, they write, and not quite well enough.
opt.conclave.say.2 [4db135] = “我们很遗憾。”信上说，你的面试表现不错，只是还差一点。
# en: "We are pleased." You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer in spell research under the Seven Towers.
opt.conclave.say.3 [b0dd08] = “我们很高兴。”你把信读了一遍又一遍，直到火漆裂开。一整个夏天，在七塔之下研究法术。
# en: "We regret." The interview went well, they write, and not quite well enough.
opt.conclave.say.4 [4db135] = “我们很遗憾。”信上说，你的面试表现不错，只是还差一点。
# en: "We regret." They wanted a GPA of 3.0, and they say so twice.
opt.conclave.say.5 [fa762a] = “我们很遗憾。”他们要的是 GPA 3.0，而且说了两遍。
# en: Letter from the Alchemists' Works
opt.alchemists.label [3ad0f0] = 炼金师工坊的来信
# en: They asked for a GPA of 2.0. The interview tests alchemy.
opt.alchemists.hint [0b2080] = 他们要求 GPA 2.0。面试考炼金。
# en: "We are pleased." You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer in the great vats of the Guild.
opt.alchemists.say.1 [d15c64] = “我们很高兴。”你把信读了一遍又一遍，直到火漆裂开。一整个夏天，守着公会的大缸。
# en: "We regret." The interview went well, they write, and not quite well enough.
opt.alchemists.say.2 [4db135] = “我们很遗憾。”信上说，你的面试表现不错，只是还差一点。
# en: "We regret." They wanted a GPA of 2.0, and they say so twice.
opt.alchemists.say.3 [1f5965] = “我们很遗憾。”他们要的是 GPA 2.0，而且说了两遍。
# en: Letter from the Expedition
opt.expedition.label [ca58f7] = 远征队的来信
# en: The interview tests vigor.
opt.expedition.hint [0bd21d] = 面试考体魄。
# en: "We are pleased." You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer of sky charts on the high plateau.
opt.expedition.say.1 [9d271b] = “我们很高兴。”你把信读了一遍又一遍，直到火漆裂开。一整个夏天，在高原上绘制星图。
# en: "We regret." The interview went well, they write, and not quite well enough.
opt.expedition.say.2 [4db135] = “我们很遗憾。”信上说，你的面试表现不错，只是还差一点。
# en: Letter from the Field Station
opt.field.label [b25fe8] = 野外站的来信
# en: The interview tests vigor.
opt.field.hint [0bd21d] = 面试考体魄。
# en: "We are pleased." You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer in the moors, the heather and the creatures in them.
opt.field.say.1 [27ceb5] = “我们很高兴。”你把信读了一遍又一遍，直到火漆裂开。一整个夏天，在荒原和石楠丛里，与那里的生灵为伴。
# en: "We regret." The interview went well, they write, and not quite well enough.
opt.field.say.2 [4db135] = “我们很遗憾。”信上说，你的面试表现不错，只是还差一点。
# en: Letter from Thornwick
opt.thornwick.label [c344dc] = 荆木学院的来信
# en: They asked for a GPA of 2.5. The interview tests charm.
opt.thornwick.hint [5c32c3] = 他们要求 GPA 2.5。面试考魅力。
# en: "We are pleased." You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer in the rival academy's illusion laboratory.
opt.thornwick.say.1 [64ec58] = “我们很高兴。”你把信读了一遍又一遍，直到火漆裂开。一整个夏天，待在对手学院的幻术实验室里。
# en: "We regret." The interview went well, they write, and not quite well enough.
opt.thornwick.say.2 [4db135] = “我们很遗憾。”信上说，你的面试表现不错，只是还差一点。
# en: "We regret." They wanted a GPA of 2.5, and they say so twice.
opt.thornwick.say.3 [ee2e12] = “我们很遗憾。”他们要的是 GPA 2.5，而且说了两遍。
# en: Open the plain envelope
opt.unseen.label [ca484a] = 拆开那只素信封
# en: Inside: a time, an address and no signature. The paper is blank again by morning. You go anyway.
opt.unseen.say.1 [702952] = 里面写着一个时间、一个地址，没有署名。到第二天早上，纸又变成了白纸。你还是去了。
# en: Fold the letters away
opt.decline.label [15c522] = 把信都收起来
# en: You fold them carefully. Next year, perhaps.
opt.decline.say.1 [b0ac8d] = 你把信仔细折好。也许明年吧。

@event intern_asked_back
# en: Asked Back
title [8aa9d6] = 再次相邀
# en: A letter from {member(intern_royal_library): the Royal Library Archives|{member(intern_conclave): the Conclave Laboratory|{member(intern_alchemists): the Guild of Alchemists' Works|{member(intern_expedition): the Observatory Expedition|{member(intern_field_station): the Beastcraft Field Station|{member(intern_thornwick): the Thornwick Exchange|the office with no name}}}}}}. They were pleased with your summer, and the post is yours again next summer if you want it.
text [92bde8] = 一封来自{member(intern_royal_library): 皇家图书馆档案馆|{member(intern_conclave): 七塔议会实验室|{member(intern_alchemists): 炼金师公会工坊|{member(intern_expedition): 观星远征队|{member(intern_field_station): 驭兽术野外站|{member(intern_thornwick): 荆木学院交换项目|那间没有名字的办公室}}}}}}的信。他们对你这个夏天很满意，只要你愿意，明年夏天这个岗位还是你的。
# en: A letter on good paper with a familiar seal, the words "next summer" underlined once, neatly.
scene [522edb] = 一封用上好纸张写的信，盖着熟悉的火漆，“明年夏天”几个字下面工整地划了一道线。
# en: Write back yes
opt.left.label [622f58] = 回信答应
# en: {~You write back the same evening. Next summer is spoken for, and you find you're glad.|"Yes," you write, and then three more lines to make it sound less eager.}
opt.left.say.1 [71669f] = {~你当晚就回了信。明年夏天有着落了，你发现自己挺高兴。|你写下“好的”，又添了三行，好让自己显得没那么迫不及待。}
# en: Thank them, and decline
opt.right.label [1b8626] = 致谢，婉拒
# en: {~You thank them warmly and say no. Next summer is yours to spend, or to apply for something new.|A polite no. You keep the letter anyway; it's good to be asked.}
opt.right.say.1 [a75a4d] = {~你热情地道谢，然后说不。明年夏天由你自己安排，或者去申请些新的。|一句礼貌的拒绝。信你还是留着了；被人邀请总是好事。}

@event thesis_setup
# en: Choosing a Thesis
title [ed9c10] = 选定论文
# en: The final year opens with a thesis. Before you choose this term's courses, Professor Thorne lays out three topics, at three levels of ambition.
text [c76290] = 最后一年以毕业论文开场。在你选定本学期的课程之前，索恩教授摆出了三个题目，野心各不相同。
# en: A professor's study, three topic proposals laid out on the desk like cards.
scene [82a455] = 教授的书房，三份选题提案像纸牌一样摊在桌上。
# en: A careful survey
opt.safe.label [d4d296] = 一篇稳妥的综述
# en: Easier, and it will read as easier.
opt.safe.hint [8d81c3] = 更容易，读起来也会显得更容易。
# en: A sensible topic. Thorne says "Sensible," the way other people say "Disappointing."
opt.safe.say.1 [5a3672] = 一个明智的题目。索恩说“明智”的语气，就像别人说“失望”。
# en: An original study
opt.solid.label [0d9f34] = 一项原创研究
# en: The usual path.
opt.solid.hint [8adec9] = 寻常的路。
# en: Thorne nods. "Good. Bring me something I don't already know."
opt.solid.say.1 [9feb76] = 索恩点点头。“好。给我带来点我还不知道的东西。”
# en: Something no one has done
opt.ambitious.label [326da2] = 前无古人的课题
# en: Harder, and worth more.
opt.ambitious.hint [83c12d] = 更难，也更有分量。
# en: Thorne is quiet for a long time. "Hm," he says, and for once it sounds like hope.
opt.ambitious.say.1 [18b887] = 索恩沉默了很久。“嗯，”他说，这一次听起来竟像是希望。

@event thesis_crunch
# en: The Crunch
title [5ad669] = 最后冲刺
# en: The defence is next month and your thesis is not ready. Your advisor's note is three words long: "Well? Final draft."
text [db90b3] = 答辩就在下个月，你的论文还没写完。导师的便条只有短短一句："如何？交终稿。"
# en: A thesis carrel at dawn, a candle burned to a stub, drafts on the floor and a student asleep on the keyboard of a typing-quill.
scene [d2cdf9] = 黎明时分的论文隔间，蜡烛燃成了残根，草稿散落一地，一名学生趴在打字羽毛笔的键盘上睡着了。
# en: Work through the nights
opt.left.label [ec1e9d] = 通宵赶工
# en: You stop seeing daylight. The draft gets better and you get worse, which seems to be how this works.
opt.left.say.1 [2f566c] = 你再也见不到日光。稿子越改越好，你却越来越糟，事情大概就是这样。
# en: Hand in what you have
opt.right.label [648c9a] = 有多少交多少
# en: You tidy what's there and accept the gaps. Your advisor sighs, which is not the same as no.
opt.right.say.1 [5cc846] = 你把现有的整理好，接受那些空缺。导师叹了口气——叹气不等于拒绝。

@event thesis_defence
# en: The Defence
title [3a2f48] = 答辩
# en: Three examiners, one lectern, and a year of work. {progress(thesis) >= 60: You know this material better than anyone in the room.|There are gaps, and you know where they are.} First, you present. Then they ask.
text [9ab052] = 三位考官，一座讲台，一年的心血。{progress(thesis) >= 60: 这些内容你比屋里任何人都熟。|有漏洞，而且你知道它们在哪儿。} 先是你陈述。然后他们提问。
# en: A semicircular table with three examiners, a student standing at a lectern with a stack of notes.
scene [f8606f] = 半圆形的长桌后坐着三位考官，一名学生站在讲台前，手里一摞笔记。
# en: Defend it
opt.left.label [0249ce] = 为它辩护
# en: A safe topic is easier to defend and earns less; an ambitious one is harder and earns more. A year of thesis work counts.
opt.left.hint [fa3c91] = 稳妥的题目更好答辩，回报也更少；大胆的题目更难，回报也更多。一年的论文功夫也会算数。
# en: Your presentation runs clean from first slide to last. One examiner has stopped taking notes and is just listening.
opt.left.say.1 [f074e0] = 你的陈述从头到尾干净利落。一位考官已经不再记笔记，只是在听。
# en: A solid presentation with one wobble in the middle. You recover. They noticed the wobble.
opt.left.say.2 [c4010c] = 一次扎实的陈述，中间晃了一下。你稳住了。他们注意到了那一下。
# en: You lose your place twice and your nerve once. The examiners exchange a look you'll remember for years.
opt.left.say.3 [6f66d2] = 你两次讲丢了位置，一次丢了胆子。考官们交换了一个你会记很多年的眼神。
# en: A careful survey, carefully presented. Nobody could fault a word of it. Nobody looks thrilled, either.
opt.left.say.4 [867002] = 一份严谨的综述，严谨地陈述。一个字都挑不出错。也没人显得激动。
# en: Careful, competent and a little dull, and you can see one examiner fighting a yawn.
opt.left.say.5 [02b389] = 严谨、称职，还有点乏味，你能看见一位考官在忍住哈欠。
# en: Even a safe topic has its gaps, and your presentation walks straight into one of them.
opt.left.say.6 [b10848] = 稳妥的题目也有漏洞，而你的陈述径直走进了其中一个。
# en: Something no one has done, laid out so clearly they can't look away. One examiner has put down their pen.
opt.left.say.7 [33edc7] = 前人从未做过的事，讲得清清楚楚，让他们移不开眼睛。一位考官放下了笔。
# en: They follow you most of the way, arguing among themselves about whether it's brilliant or mad. Possibly both.
opt.left.say.8 [c3424d] = 他们大半程都跟上了你，彼此争论这究竟是天才还是疯狂。也许两者都是。
# en: You reach too far in the first ten minutes, and spend the rest of the hour trying to get back. They let you.
opt.left.say.9 [8a9009] = 你在头十分钟就走得太远，剩下的一个小时都在设法往回走。他们由着你。
# en: And under the presentation, a year of work they can feel. Every page they turn has been turned before.
opt.left.say.10 [90a675] = 陈述之下，是他们能感觉到的一整年功夫。他们翻过的每一页，你都早已翻过。
# en: Under the presentation, the thin chapters show. One examiner starts counting pages.
opt.left.say.11 [cbd512] = 陈述之下，单薄的章节露了馅。一位考官开始数页数。
# en: Open with your weakest chapter
opt.right.label [dd91ef] = 从最薄弱的一章讲起
# en: Name the gaps before they find them. Safe, and modest.
opt.right.hint [047c2c] = 在他们发现之前先说出漏洞。稳妥，也平淡。
# en: You start with what you couldn't prove, and why, and what you'd do next. It takes the wind out of their sails, and a little out of yours.
opt.right.say.1 [e57cc7] = 你从无法证明的部分讲起，讲为什么，讲下一步会怎么做。这让他们泄了气，也让你泄了一点气。
# en: The rest of it stands on a year of real work, and they can tell.
opt.right.say.2 [f4fa42] = 其余部分立在一整年扎实的功夫上，他们看得出来。
# en: The trouble is how many chapters are weak. They notice that too.
opt.right.say.3 [3088c9] = 麻烦在于薄弱的章节太多了。这一点他们也注意到了。

@event thesis_defence_question
# en: The Question
title [b2a4e8] = 那个问题
# en: The examiner who hasn't spoken yet opens your thesis to a page near the end, puts a finger on one line and asks the question you hoped no one would ask.
text [f3f712] = 那位一直没开口的考官把你的论文翻到靠后的一页，手指按在一行字上，问出了你最希望没人问的那个问题。
# en: An examiner leaning over a semicircular table, pointing at one line in a thick bound thesis, the student at the lectern very still.
scene [24c9e8] = 一位考官俯身在半圆形的桌子上，指着一本厚厚的装订论文中的一行，讲台旁的学生一动不动。
# en: Answer it head-on
opt.left.label [f11e30] = 正面回答
# en: You answer it, and then the question behind it, and then the one behind that. The examiner closes the thesis, slowly.
opt.left.say.1 [298ca3] = 你回答了它，然后回答了它背后的问题，然后是再背后的那个。考官慢慢合上了论文。
# en: Your answer starts well and ends somewhere you didn't mean to go. The examiner lets the silence do the rest.
opt.left.say.2 [90a716] = 你的回答开头很好，结尾却去了一个你没打算去的地方。考官让沉默替自己说完了剩下的话。
# en: Admit what you don't know
opt.right.label [cb596c] = 承认你不知道的
# en: "I don't know," you say, "and here is how I'd find out." From someone who has just presented so well, it sounds like mastery. Two examiners nod.
opt.right.say.1 [ce3f4f] = “我不知道，”你说，“但我会这样去弄清楚。”出自一个刚刚陈述得如此出色的人之口，这听起来像是驾轻就熟。两位考官点了点头。
# en: "I don't know," you say, "and here is how I'd find out." It stings a little, and earns you nothing. The examiner moves on.
opt.right.say.2 [875e12] = “我不知道，”你说，“但我会这样去弄清楚。”这让你有点难受，也没给你加分。考官继续往下问了。

@event thesis_defence_verdict
# en: The Verdict
title [5a8455] = 结果
# en: They send you out. Twenty minutes on a bench in the corridor, with the clock and your heartbeat. Then the door opens, and they call you back in.
text [1f091a] = 他们请你出去。在走廊的长椅上等了二十分钟，只有钟声和你的心跳。然后门开了，他们叫你回去。
# en: A student waiting alone on a bench in a long stone corridor outside a closed oak door, hands clasped, a clock on the wall.
scene [bef3d0] = 一个学生独自坐在长长的石头走廊里的长椅上，紧闭的橡木门外，双手紧握，墙上挂着一只钟。
# en: Go back in
opt.ok.label [b89225] = 回去
# en: They stop asking questions and start asking for copies. Distinction. One of them shakes your hand twice, as if the first didn't count.
opt.ok.say.1 [9fca70] = 他们不再提问，开始讨要副本。优等。其中一位和你握了两次手，好像第一次不算数。
# en: A pass, with one examiner's handwriting all over your conclusion. "Good work," says the chair, and means it, mostly.
opt.ok.say.2 [efa14a] = 通过了，只是结论部分写满了某位考官的批注。“干得好，”主席说，大体上是真心的。
# en: They send you away to resubmit. It isn't the end. It feels like it. The idea was good, says the chair. The proof wasn't there yet.
opt.ok.say.3 [c92bcd] = 他们让你回去重交。这不是终点。只是感觉像。主席说，想法是好的。只是证明还没到位。

@event lantern_night_v3
# en: Lantern Night
title [0b1f19] = 灯笼夜
# en: Lantern Night. The whole academy gathers on the lakeshore with paper lanterns, each carrying a wish out over the water. {month == 2 and year == 1: Your first one.|Another year, another wish.}
text [b3014a] = 灯笼夜。全院的人带着纸灯笼聚在湖岸，每盏灯都载着一个愿望飘向水面。{month == 2 and year == 1: 这是你的第一次。|又一年，又一个愿望。}
# en: The Mirror Lake at night, hundreds of paper lanterns drifting over the water, students crowding the shore.
scene [cd9b4c] = 夜晚的镜湖，数百盏纸灯笼在水面上漂，学生们挤满湖岸。
# en: Wish for something selfish
opt.left.label [7e0393] = 许一个自私的愿望
# en: Your lantern goes out over the water and keeps its secret. You feel lighter for having asked.
opt.left.say.1 [0210ff] = 你的灯笼飘向湖面，守着它的秘密。问出口之后，你觉得轻松了些。
# en: Wish for someone else
opt.right.label [bc6686] = 为别人许愿
# en: You don't tell anyone who. The lantern seems to know; it flies straight.
opt.right.say.1 [00b286] = 你没告诉任何人是谁。灯笼似乎知道，它飞得笔直。

@event year_four
# en: The Final Year
title [a30775] = 最后一年
# en: The barge again, the towers again, and a thesis waiting. The first-years on the deck look at you the way you once looked at the fourth-years. At the opening feast the headmistress says, "Fourth years, this is your last year in these halls. What you become here, you will be for a long time." She looks, for a moment, directly at you.
text [cb5447] = 又是驳船，又是高塔，还有一篇论文在等着。甲板上的一年级生看你的眼神，就像你当年看四年级生那样。开学宴上，院长说：“四年级的同学们，这是你们在这些厅堂里的最后一年。你们在这里成为什么样的人，就会长久地是那样的人。”有那么一刻，她直直地看着你。
# en: The seven towers at dawn from the barge, the same view as the first day, but the student watching it has changed.
scene [542188] = 从驳船上望见的黎明七塔，和第一天的景色一样，但看风景的学生已经变了。
# en: Here we go
opt.ok.label [e1aa95] = 走吧
# en: You know which steps creak and which doors stick. The thesis will want evenings of its own each term; something else may have to give, a club or a job.
opt.ok.say.1 [e66c41] = 你知道哪级台阶会响，哪扇门会卡。毕业论文每学期都要占去好些晚上；总得放下点什么，一个社团，或者一份工作。

@event grade_appeal
# en: The Appeal
title [83680b] = 申诉
# en: The examiners' list is pinned up, and beside {track} there is an F. The clerk mentions, without looking up, that a student may appeal a grade in person, once, before the board. Most don't. Some of those who do come out with a C.
text [dc09dc] = 考官名单贴出来了，{track}旁边是一个 F。办事员头也不抬地提了一句：学生可以亲自向委员会申诉一次成绩。大多数人不去。去了的人里，有些拿回了一个 C。
# en: A long table of grey-robed examiners in a panelled room, a single student standing before them holding an exam paper.
scene [ba2029] = 镶着护墙板的房间里，一长排身穿灰袍的考官坐在桌后，一个学生拿着考卷独自站在他们面前。
# en: Appeal before the board
opt.left.label [fecb7e] = 向委员会申诉
# en: You talk for ten minutes about the paper, the question and the answer they marked wrong. The board confers in whispers. The F becomes a C, in red ink, with a sigh.
opt.left.say.1 [20d3bd] = 你就那张考卷、那道题和那个被判错的答案讲了十分钟。委员会低声商议。F 变成了 C，红墨水写的，附带一声叹气。
# en: The board hears you out, then reads your paper aloud. It's worse aloud. The F stands, and the queue outside the door heard every word.
opt.left.say.2 [63e52e] = 委员会听完你的话，然后把你的考卷念了一遍。念出来更糟。F 维持原判，门外排队的人一字不落全听见了。
# en: Accept it, and read the comments
opt.right.label [b758f4] = 接受成绩，读读评语
# en: The examiner's comments are fair, which is the worst thing about them. You copy out every one. Next time you'll know exactly where it went wrong.
opt.right.say.1 [1fbf52] = 考官的评语很公道，这正是最糟的地方。你一条一条抄下来。下次你会清楚地知道自己错在哪儿。

@event registrar_list
# en: The Registrar's List
title [0ca2e7] = 教务处的课程表
# en: Before enrolment, the registrar's list goes up in the entrance hall: each course, what it tests, which spells it teaches, and which open only next term. A second-year taps one. "That one's hard," she says, then taps another. "So's that."
text [f5996f] = 选课前，教务处的课程表贴在了门厅：每门课考什么，教哪些咒语，哪些下学期才开。一个二年级生点了点其中一门。“这门难，”她说，又点了另一门，“这门也难。”
# en: A crowd of new students around a long parchment list pinned in an entrance hall, one of them tracing a line with a finger.
scene [ddd05b] = 门厅里一群新生围着一张长长的羊皮纸名单，其中一个用手指顺着一行往下划。
# en: Read it twice
opt.ok.label [7de276] = 看两遍
# en: Two courses a term, a fee each time, and an exam at the end of each. Pass a level and you learn its spells.
opt.ok.say.1 [fb0418] = 每学期两门课，每次都要交课程费，每学期末各有一场考试。通过一个级别，就能学会它的咒语。

@event club_fair_flyer
# en: Flyers Under the Door
title [fb904d] = 门缝下的传单
# en: One flyer slides under your door, then another, then nine. The Club Fair is next month in the courtyard: the Duelling Circle, the Lumen Ledger, the Verdant Circle. One club at a time, says the small print, and each wants a couple of evenings a term.
text [f8867e] = 一张传单从门缝下塞进来，又一张，然后是九张。社团招新会下个月在庭院举行：决斗社、《流明纪事报》社、青翠社。小字写着：一次只能加入一个社团，每个社团每学期要占你几个晚上。
# en: A dormitory floor scattered with colourful club flyers, more sliding under the door as a student watches.
scene [f482c7] = 宿舍地板上散落着五颜六色的社团传单，还有更多正从门缝下塞进来，一个学生在一旁看着。
# en: Keep the flyers
opt.ok.label [e3ac1e] = 把传单留着
# en: You pin them over your bed and argue with them until you fall asleep.
opt.ok.say.1 [ce52b4] = 你把它们钉在床头，和它们争论到睡着。

@event job_board_notice
# en: Hands Wanted
title [82086c] = 招人
# en: Pinned to the refectory door: "Hands wanted. See the Job Board, entrance hall." Under it, in pencil: "The Newt pays best. The library is warmest." Under that, in a third hand: "Pell counts."
text [eb646b] = 膳堂门上钉着：“招人。详见门厅招工告示板。”下面有人用铅笔写：“酒馆给钱最多。图书馆最暖和。”再下面是第三种笔迹：“佩尔要数数。”
# en: A refectory door with a notice pinned to it, three different handwritings added beneath the printed part.
scene [ee5aec] = 膳堂门上钉着一张告示，印刷字下面添了三种不同的笔迹。
# en: Make a note of it
opt.ok.label [70f916] = 记下来
# en: One job at a time, a few shifts a term, paid by the shift. The board is up from morning until evening.
opt.ok.say.1 [611dbe] = 一次只能做一份工，每学期几个班次，按班次付钱。告示板从早上一直开到傍晚。
